'@@author Atharva005
@startuml
title Validate an activity schedule before insertion or replacement
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EDF3F8
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #526477
skinparam ArrowColor #526477
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor "User" as User
participant "ui:Ui" as UI
participant ConsoleHelper as Console
participant "add:AddCommand" as Add
participant ActivityScheduleValidator as Validator
participant "activities:ActivityList" as Activities

Console -> UI : readLine()
User -> UI : add ...
UI --> Console : input

Console -> Add : execute(activities, storage)
Add -> Validator : validate(candidate, activities, null, allowOverlap)
Validator -> Activities : getCanonicalView()
Activities --> Validator : chronological activities
note over Validator, Activities
  Duplicate identity: equal date, start and end,
  and equal names ignoring case and surrounding whitespace.
  Demand, ratings and completion do not change duplicate identity.
  Inspect records in chronological order to report the first conflicting index.
end note

alt duplicate identity exists
  Validator --> Add : throws UniEnableException(duplicate warning)
  Add --> Console : propagate warning
  Console -> UI : showMessage(warning)
  UI --> User : warning
else no duplicate
  alt allowOverlap is true
    Validator --> Add : validation passed
  else same-date positive overlap exists
    note over Validator, Activities
      candidate.start < existing.end AND existing.start < candidate.end.
      Equal endpoints are allowed; completed activities still participate.
    end note
    Validator --> Add : throws UniEnableException(clash warning and overlap/ALLOW hint)
    Add --> Console : propagate warning
    Console -> UI : showMessage(warning)
    UI --> User : warning
  else no clash
    Validator --> Add : validation passed
  end
end

opt validation passed
  Add -> Activities : addActivity(candidate)
  Activities --> Add : activity inserted
  Add --> Console : CommandResult(message, false, true)
  ref over Console, UI
  automatic save and display
  CompletionAndSaveSequence
end ref
  UI --> User : confirmation or save warning
  note over Console, Activities
    The shared automatic-save and display flow follows insertion.
    Validation itself performs no mutation or file I/O.
  end note
end

note over Add, Validator
  EditCommand passes the original activity as replacedActivity and excludes only that object.
  Name/schedule edits validate before replaceByDisplayedIndex(); demand/rating-only edits skip this check.
  overlap/ALLOW skips only clash checking. Duplicate identities always remain rejected.
end note
@enduml
'@@author
